  "content": {
    "id": "p44-q37-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "37",
    "prompt": "A straight line passes through the point $(2,1)$ and has positive $x$- and $y$-intercepts at $P$ and $Q$ respectively. Suppose $\\angle OPQ=\\alpha$, where $O$ is the origin.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p44-q37-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Explain why the line has gradient $-\\tan\\alpha$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The angle of inclination is $\\pi-\\alpha$, so $m=\\tan(\\pi-\\alpha)=-\\tan\\alpha$.",
          "worked": "The angle of inclination is $\\pi-\\alpha$.\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=\\tan(\\pi-\\alpha)\\\\m&=-\\tan\\alpha\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q37-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the $x$- and $y$-intercepts in terms of $\\alpha$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P=\\left(2+\\dfrac{1}{\\tan\\alpha},0\\right)$ and $Q=(0,1+2\\tan\\alpha)$.",
          "worked": "Using $y=mx+b$ and $m=-\\tan\\alpha$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-x\\tan\\alpha+b\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting $(2,1)$,\n$$\\begin{align*}1&=-2\\tan\\alpha+b\\\\b&=1+2\\tan\\alpha\\\\y&=-x\\tan\\alpha+1+2\\tan\\alpha\\end{align*}$$\nAt the $x$-intercept, $y=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}0&=-x\\tan\\alpha+1+2\\tan\\alpha\\\\x\\tan\\alpha&=1+2\\tan\\alpha\\\\x&=\\frac{1}{\\tan\\alpha}+2\\end{align*}$$\nThus $P=\\left(\\dfrac{1}{\\tan\\alpha}+2,0\\right)$.\nAt the $y$-intercept, $x=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=0+1+2\\tan\\alpha\\\\y&=1+2\\tan\\alpha\\end{align*}$$\nThus $Q=(0,2\\tan\\alpha+1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 57
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q37-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Show that the area of $\\triangle OPQ$ is given by $A=\\dfrac{(2\\tan\\alpha+1)^2}{2\\tan\\alpha}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=\\dfrac12(2\\tan\\alpha+1)\\left(2+\\dfrac1{\\tan\\alpha}\\right)=\\dfrac{(2\\tan\\alpha+1)^2}{2\\tan\\alpha}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12bh\\\\A&=\\frac12(2\\tan\\alpha+1)\\left(\\frac1{\\tan\\alpha}+2\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac12(2\\tan\\alpha+1)\\left(\\frac{1+2\\tan\\alpha}{\\tan\\alpha}\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac{(2\\tan\\alpha+1)^2}{2\\tan\\alpha}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q37-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "By letting $u=\\tan\\alpha$, find $\\dfrac{dA}{du}$ and hence show that this area is minimised when $\\tan\\alpha=\\dfrac12$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{dA}{du}=\\dfrac{(2u-1)(2u+1)}{2u^2}$. Its sign changes from negative to positive at $u=\\dfrac12$, so the area is minimised when $\\tan\\alpha=\\dfrac12$.",
          "worked": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p44-q37-d-work-intro",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Let ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "u=\\tan\\alpha",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". Since α is acute, u > 0.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p44-q37-d-work-derivative",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{(2u+1)^2}{2u}\\\\\\frac{dA}{du}&=\\frac{2(2u+1)(2)(2u)-(2u+1)^2(2)}{4u^2}\\\\\\frac{dA}{du}&=\\frac{(2u-1)(2u+1)}{2u^2}\\end{align*}",
                    "display": true
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p44-q37-d-work-stationary",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "At a stationary point,",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\begin{align*}\\frac{dA}{du}&=0\\\\(2u-1)(2u+1)&=0\\\\u&=\\frac12\\text{ or }-\\frac12\\end{align*}",
                    "display": true
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p44-q37-d-work-domain",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Since ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "u>0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", only ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "u=\\frac12",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " is in the domain. Check using a table of slopes:",
                    "marks": []
